Let me look at the shuffle function and understand the vulnerability. The key issue is in the `BLOSC_SHUFFLE` case in `pipeline_forward`:

```c
case BLOSC_SHUFFLE:
  for (int j = 0; j <= filters_meta[i]; j++) {
    shuffle(typesize, bsize, _src, _dest);
    // Cycle filters when required
    if (j < filters_meta[i]) {
      _src = _dest;
      _dest = _tmp;
      _tmp = _src;
    }
  }
  break;
```

The `filters_meta[i]` is set from `data[1]` in the fuzzer. If `filters_meta[i]` is large, the shuffle loop runs many times. But the buffers `_tmp` and `_dest` are only allocated for `bsize` bytes. Let me check how the tmp buffers are allocated.

